Setup

Backend (Django):
cd backend
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py runserver

Frontend (React), in a separate terminal:
cd frontend
npm install
npm start

Backend runs on http://localhost:8000
Frontend runs on http://localhost:3000

What's working right now:
- View list of drivers assigned to a sponsor
- View a single driver's details
- Approve a pending driver

Add a test driver:
Go to http://localhost:8000/api/sponsor/drivers/ in your browser, fill out the form at the bottom (Name, Sponsor id, Status), click POST.

Note: sponsor ID is currently hardcoded to 1 as a placeholder until login/auth exists.






*** TO CONNECT TO DATABASE ***
export RDSHOST="database-1.cluster-cobd8enwsupz.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com" 
psql "host=$RDSHOST port=5432 dbname=postgres user=postgres sslmode=require password=$(aws rds generate-db-auth-token --hostname $RDSHOST --port 5432 --username postgres --region us-east-1)"
